REMARK 280                                                                      
REMARK 280 CRYSTALLIZATION CONDITIONS: PURIFIED PAPS REDUCTASE FROM             
REMARK 280  METHANOTHERMOCOCCUS THERMOLITHOTROPHICUS AT A CONCENTRATION OF      
REMARK 280  20 MG.ML-1 WAS ANAEROBICALLY CRYSTALLIZED INSIDE A COY TENT (N2/    
REMARK 280  H2 AT A 96:4 RATIO) UNDER YELLOW LIGHT CONDITION. 0.7 UL OF         
REMARK 280  PAPSR IN 25 MM TRIS/HCL PH 7.6, 2 MM DITHIOTHREITOL, 0.5 MM FAD,    
REMARK 280  AND 10 % V/V GLYCEROL WAS MIXED WITH 0.7 UL RESERVOIR SOLUTION.     
REMARK 280  THE DROPS WERE SPOTTED IN A 96-WELL MRC 2-DROP CRYSTALLIZATION      
REMARK 280  PLATES IN POLYSTYRENE (SWISSCI) CONTAINING 90 UL OF                 
REMARK 280  CRYSTALLIZATION SOLUTION IN THE RESERVOIR. CRYSTALS APPEARED        
REMARK 280  AFTER A FEW DAYS IN THE FOLLOWING CRYSTALLIZATION CONDITION: 35 %   
REMARK 280  V/V 2-METHYL-2,4-PENTANEDIOL, 100 MM TRIS PH 7.0 AND 200 MM         
REMARK 280  NACL. PRIOR TO TRANSFER TO LIQUID NITROGEN, THE CRYSTAL WAS         
REMARK 280  SOAKED IN 10 MM DISODIUM 3'-PHOSPHOADENOSINE 5'-PHOSPHATE FOR 7     
REMARK 280  MIN., VAPOR DIFFUSION, SITTING DROP, TEMPERATURE 293K               
